    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d102">

                <pb facs="0247" n="191" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg191"/>

                <head>(M. 3294.)<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Messrs. D. &amp;
                            C. MacIver to Board of
                    Trade</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British and North American Royal Mail Steam-Packet
                                Company</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Office</hi> 8 <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Water Street, Liverpool</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1875-02-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 24, 1875</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your communication of the 19th
                    instant, we beg to say that we have referred the matter to Messrs. Burns, of
                    Glasgow, and that their reply to a similar communication from you sufficiently
                    expresses our views upon the subject.</p>
                <p>Yours, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed><list>
                            <item>D. &amp; C. M<hi rendition="#small-caps">ac</hi>IVER,</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#italic">Pro</hi> E. M<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                    >ac</hi>IVER, <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jr</hi>.</item>
                        </list></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Board of Trade</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
